From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:39:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] lab(uefi): receipt-gated tool gateway in the mint path
 (CALC, LOOKUP over a declared TABLE.TSV)

The mint path can now run one tool step with no OS underneath, mirroring
aegis-linux/examples/agent_trace.rs: the scanner takes the earliest CALC( or
LOOKUP( opener in the model's newly decoded text, parses only that one,
evaluates it (checked i64 arithmetic with the gateway's fixed error strings;
table lookup with the literal NONE on a miss; LOOKUP is not scanned for
unless TABLE.TSV is declared), appends "\nTOOL[<name>]=<output>\n" to the
prompt and decodes a second step.

- gateway.rs (new): grammar, eval_calc, table parsing, run_tool,
  tool_result_text, call_line_complete.
- verifier.rs: replay_with's observer may now return `true` to end the decode
  early; decode_tokens() helper. replay() unchanged in behaviour.
- main.rs: TABLE.TSV loaded (<= 64 KiB) and measured into PCR 12 when present;
  step 0 stops after a complete call line, step 1 at end-of-text; after an
  early stop the canonical decode is re-run for exactly that many tokens so
  RECEIPT.TXT / RECEIPT2.TXT are plain witness v1 receipts (maxtok == gen-toks)
  that cis_witness verify accepts unchanged; the second receipt's chain is
  extended into PCR 13 ("mint-tool"); dashboard shows the tool line and both
  receipt summaries.

QEMU gate (swtpm): calc and lookup prompts exit 33; all four receipts replay
bit-for-bit on Linux (cis_witness verify PASS); attest_verify.py reports
ATTEST VERIFY PASS and QUOTE VERIFY PASS with the TABLE.TSV event in PCR 12
and two receipt events in PCR 13. Verify mode is unchanged. No performance
claims (Rule A).

